## defaults (no FM_TASK_INBOX_* in env)
0
grace=90 ring_max=3 busy_max=2

## scaffold a ship brief in a disposable FM_HOME
--- inbox section as the worker sees it:
# Firstmate instruction inbox
Firstmate steers you through durable message files in '/tmp/fm-brief-drive.XaRnDX/state/ship.inbox'.
When a terminal message says an instruction is waiting there - and at any natural checkpoint when you are unsure - list them with `find '/tmp/fm-brief-drive.XaRnDX/state/ship.inbox' -maxdepth 1 -name '*.msg' 2>/dev/null | sort -V` and read the complete contents of each record (including its final line even when it is not newline-terminated) in numeric order.
Prefer the format-aware `fm_task_inbox_body` reader from `bin/fm-task-inbox-lib.sh` when it is available. If you read manually, a header line `body-terminator=1` means the writer added exactly one synthetic final newline to terminate the record file; that marked newline is not part of the logical message body, so remove only it and preserve any intentional trailing newlines. Legacy records without that marker may end without a newline; read them through the file end.
Immediately after reading each message, before acting, record that you read it: `'/home/firstmate/.no-mistakes/worktrees/5284051b2355/01M5Q99RTNBFRDXBK2ZC9NVJE2/bin/fm-task-inbox-read.sh' '/tmp/fm-brief-drive.XaRnDX/state/ship.inbox'/NNN.msg`.
Do not record a read before actually reading the message.
If the command fails or cannot run, use your file tools to create /tmp/fm-brief-drive.XaRnDX/state/ship.inbox/.read/ if needed, then create the empty receipt /tmp/fm-brief-drive.XaRnDX/state/ship.inbox/.read/NNN.msg for the message you just read.
Report a read-acknowledgement failure only if the file-tool fallback also fails; never assume a failed write acknowledged the message.
Then act on the message and acknowledge completed handling by moving it: `mv '/tmp/fm-brief-drive.XaRnDX/state/ship.inbox'/NNN.msg '/tmp/fm-brief-drive.XaRnDX/state/ship.inbox'/handled/`.
The read receipt stops unread-instruction alarms while you work; it does not mean the work is complete or replace the handled/ move.
An empty or absent inbox needs no action.

## firstmate steers the worker (real record write) and the watcher sees it unread
record=/tmp/fm-brief-drive.XaRnDX/state/ship.inbox/001.msg
due_action(grace=0) before any read: ring /tmp/fm-brief-drive.XaRnDX/state/ship.inbox/001.msg

## worker runs the brief's receipt command verbatim (NNN -> 001)
command: '/home/firstmate/.no-mistakes/worktrees/5284051b2355/01M5Q99RTNBFRDXBK2ZC9NVJE2/bin/fm-task-inbox-read.sh' '/tmp/fm-brief-drive.XaRnDX/state/ship.inbox'/001.msg
exit=0
total 0
